+
+### Local standing-head calibration (control.48-head-bmi088.4, API 45)
+
+The `head_bmi088` commissioning extension uses contract `head_mount_standing_v2` and
+calibration C ABI v2 (352-byte status); the estimator ABI v1 is unchanged. A settled
+`hold-home` keeps all joints powered. Only the commissioning Hold writes UART targets;
+`head_imu_standing.rs` schedules automatic static captures and bounded head trajectories.
+
+`head-imu-calibration` accepts `start`, `status`, `resume`, `test`, `pause`, `cancel`, and
+`save`. Start only collects the standing/forward/back/left/right sequence. Test requires
+separate operator confirmation after the robot is placed back on the table, still
+standing; it captures a fresh standing baseline then tests ID30–33 in sequence at about
+±5 degrees. Source data and encoder feedback come from the real providers, not clients.
+Status renews a 2.5-second foreground lease but never resumes paused work. Timeout,
+missing data or follow error pauses the trajectory; normal stop freezes the active head
+joint at measured position and retains body Hold. Relax/power requests still cut torque
+through the original path. A paused or active run blocks unrelated calibration writes.
+
+The native report is bound to model, head zero/direction, mount and all ten measurements;
+head-motion checks also require low smoothed residual gyro energy relative to expected
+head motion, so a zero gyro cannot pass simply because the sweep is slow. Save is explicit
+and keeps policy motion disabled. To commit and restart into policy mode, the operator
+must support the robot and relax first. Fixed-body `verify-imu` still refuses this source.
